@startuml scorm-export
title SCORM export of a published module (SCORM 1.2 or 2004 4th edition)
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false

actor Author
participant "SPA\n(admin area)" as SPA
participant "Phoenix\nExportController" as Api
participant "Oban\nExportWorker" as Job
participant "Oban\nStaleExportWorker" as Sweep
participant "Catalog" as Cat
collections "Player bundle\n(priv/scorm_player)" as Bundle
database "Export storage" as Store
participant "External LMS" as LMS

Author -> SPA : choose a published module and a SCORM version
SPA -> Api : POST /api/admin/exports {module_id, scorm_version}
Api -> Job : enqueue export
Api --> SPA : 202 export (status queued)
Job -> Cat : load published content including answer keys
Job -> Job : write content.json
Job -> Bundle : copy player files
Job -> Job : write imsmanifest.xml (1.2 or 2004 4th edition)
Job -> Store : zip the package, then set done\nonly while the export is running
Job -> Store : delete the done exports beyond max_packages\n(the new export counts as the newest)
SPA -> Api : GET /api/admin/exports/:id
Api --> SPA : status and download link
Author -> LMS : upload the package
LMS -> LMS : launch the SCO; Scorm12Runtime calls LMSInitialize,\nScorm2004Runtime calls Initialize

== every 15 minutes ==
Sweep -> Store : set queued or running exports unchanged for twice\nthe job timeout (at least one hour) to failed, remove their files
Sweep -> Store : delete done and failed exports older than max_age_days\nand done exports beyond max_packages with their files,\nremove files without an export row
SPA -> Api : GET /api/admin/exports/:id of a deleted export
Api --> SPA : 404, shown as no longer available

note over Job, Bundle
  One module becomes one SCO. Its learning objectives
  become cmi.objectives entries (id = objective key)
  with the status of their evidence.
  Scorm12Runtime maps outcomes to cmi.core.lesson_status
  and cmi.core.score.raw. Scorm2004Runtime maps them to
  cmi.completion_status, cmi.success_status and
  cmi.score.scaled.
  The resume state must fit suspend_data: 4,096 characters
  in 1.2 and 64,000 characters in 2004.
end note

note over LMS
  The package evaluates answers locally, so it contains
  the answer keys. Anonymous insights (self-assessment,
  votes, feedback) are not part of an export.
end note
@enduml
